{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/770254-enchantment-devotion-the-charmed-condition","id":770254,"title":"Enchantment Devotion & the Charmed Condition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-20T13:34:06-08:00","id":770254,"title":"Enchantment Devotion & the Charmed Condition","content":"Does Enchantment require the vampire to inflict the Charmed Condition on the target first? It'd make sense since it's basically Loyalty with a twist, but normally that sort of thing would be explicitly listed as a requirement in a clearly labeled section next to the cost, dice pool, action type, etc. Maybe the writer considered it implicitly part of &quot;All the other parameters remain the same, but the victim insists on defending and cherishing a different person, place, or thing.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T06:57:05-08:00","id":771455,"title":"","content":"Yes they have to successfully Awe the person/people (no roll)<br /> Successfully use Confidant to charm the person/people (contested roll)<br /> Successfully use Loyalty and make them Enthralled (contested roll and cost of 2 vitae per person)<br /> Successfully activate Enchantment and designate who or what they want them to protect. (contested roll and 1 vitae per person)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T07:57:35-08:00","id":771482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/770254-enchantment-devotion-the-charmed-condition?p=771455#post771455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they have to successfully Awe the person/people (no roll)<br /> Successfully use Confidant to charm the person/people (contested roll)<br /> Successfully use Loyalty and make them Enthralled (contested roll and cost of 2 vitae per person)<br /> Successfully activate Enchantment and designate who or what they want them to protect. (contested roll and 1 vitae per person)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they have to use Loyalty to Enthrall the victim first. Enchantment says it &quot;works as Loyalty, but the vampire can designate a source for the Enthralled Condition instead of herself.&quot; So Enchantment itself should inflict the Enthralled Condition, otherwise it wouldn't be working as Loyalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T08:31:47-08:00","id":771500,"title":"","content":"Except the write up for Enchantment specifically says they are transferring the feelings invoked in the victim to to another person or object, they must communicate to the victim of enchantment who or what is to be protected/obeyed and that it keeps all the parameters required for activating Loyalty. That means the victim gets the resist check for Loyalty (Resolve + Blood Potency) in addition to to resist check for using the devotion which is Composure + Blood Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T10:33:24-08:00","id":771583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If successful, this Devotion works as Loyalty, but the vampire can designate a source for the Enthralled Condition instead of focusing it on herself. All the other parameters remain the same, but the victim insists on defending and cherishing a different person, place, or thing. She has to somehow communicate the desired subject of the Enchantment to the victim for this Devotion to work. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in there about transferring feelings, only that the vampire has to somehow indicate to the victim what the target of those feelings will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:13:02-08:00","id":771611,"title":"","content":"No I'm sorry tsusasi but there is just no way the text means that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If successful, this Devotion works as Loyalty, but the vampire can designate a source for the Enthralled Condition instead of focusing it on herself. All the other parameters remain the same, but the victim insists on defending and cherishing a different person, place, or thing. She has to somehow communicate the desired subject of the Enchantment to the victim for this Devotion to work.<br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> This means you use it i<u>nstead of </u>Loyalty and it has the exact same effect, same roll results and everything, with the exception of the target of the victim's affection and the resist check.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T12:03:39-08:00","id":771633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/770254-enchantment-devotion-the-charmed-condition?p=771583#post771583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing in there about transferring feelings, only that the vampire has to somehow indicate to the victim what the target of those feelings will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this: <br /> <i>but the vampire can designate a source for the Enthralled Condition instead of focusing it on herself </i><br /> <br /> And the first two sentences of the devotion's entry do actually state that is the effect of the power. <br /> <br /> <i>Majesty is a gift that draws attention and bends feelings toward the vampire. With this Devotion, and a bit of Obfuscate, the vampire can deflect those feelings to another person, or to a place or thing.</i> (Blood and Smoke p. 143)<br /> <br /> You can't designate the Enthralled Condition to another target if the condition doesn't exist in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T12:15:02-08:00","id":771638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/770254-enchantment-devotion-the-charmed-condition?p=771633#post771633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except this: <br /> <i>but the vampire can designate a source for the Enthralled Condition instead of focusing it on herself </i><br /> <br /> And the first two sentences of the devotion's entry do actually state that is the effect of the power. <br /> <br /> <i>Majesty is a gift that draws attention and bends feelings toward the vampire. With this Devotion, and a bit of Obfuscate, the vampire can deflect those feelings to another person, or to a place or thing.</i> (Blood and Smoke p. 143)<br /> <br /> You can't designate the Enthralled Condition to another target if the condition doesn't exist in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, again, Enchantment <i>works as Loyalty</i>, with the exception that you designate someone else as the target for the admiration brought on by Enthralled Condition. Since all Loyalty does is inflicts the Enthralled Condition (with the vampire as the target of the adoration), what exactly is Enchantment doing that's like Loyalty if not inflicting the Enthralled Condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T12:21:28-08:00","id":771643,"title":"","content":"I agree with Charlaquin and Ophion. You must Awe first, then Confidant, then you can use Enchantment, no use of Loyalty required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T12:44:03-08:00","id":774206,"title":"","content":"Why would you take a devotion that does exactly the same thing as the next step in the discipline, knowing you would have to take that too in order to get the final step? It makes no sense to me that they would write a devotion that does what the discipline does. At least all the devotions I can think of do something new that the discipline can not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:24:08-08:00","id":774312,"title":"","content":"The use of Enchantment replaces the use of Loyalty, so you don't have to roll both of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:30:15-08:00","id":774319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/770254-enchantment-devotion-the-charmed-condition?p=774206#post774206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you take a devotion that does exactly the same thing as the next step in the discipline, knowing you would have to take that too in order to get the final step? It makes no sense to me that they would write a devotion that does what the discipline does. At least all the devotions I can think of do something new that the discipline can not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I does do something the Discipline cannot. It makes someone other than the user the subject of the victim's adoration. That's something Majesty on its own can't do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:37:50-08:00","id":774324,"title":"","content":"Loyalty can only make the target Enthralled with the person using the Discipline. Enchantment makes the target Enthralled with a person, place, or thing other than the one using the Devotion. Enchantment requires Majesty 4 to learn, so anyone with Enchantment already has Loyalty. It's a niche Devotion, but there are scenarios where it may be preferable to let someone or something else take the brunt of the thrall's adoration (or the Thrall may be a gift/bargaining tool). The Vitae cost is also a bit cheaper, and it is contested by Composure instead of Resolve, though that last part probably wasn't a conscious design choice. WoD can be a bit inconsistent about when supernatural emotional manipulation is resisted/contested by Composure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":".  Second Paragraph became redundant after Rose's post 11-25-2015, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}